items.brief:
A pure MIG-01 mapper plus a read-only dry run. It writes nothing.

(1) lib/migrate/map.js maps legacy content to section 8.3 documents using the merged kind names: the 8 cms_blocks keys (header and footer honour nav null vs [] vs absent; announcement); cms_pages by family (doc_p_<hash> via backfillRouteId; policies; journal posts and index); design from config brand and theme (env config for _default); doc_cart from the cart_upsell placement (title and position kept); page_redirects attached to the target document's meta.redirect_from or reported unresolved; the surface_templates header, footer, pdp and collection entries. lib/migrate/state.js classifies the tenant per the spec 8.11 table, EXCEPT 'no release': that state needs an explicit operator flag, storeOpen: true|false (--store-open / --not-launched); without it the mapper returns a refusal 'needs --store-open or --not-launched' and never guesses. It honours every trap: sec_l<i> and i-<n> ids kept, the materialized half of a half-customized doc_home with a {store_name} binding, sections without a kind become text, code-default pages. Values that fail strict validation or exceed limits are carried verbatim with inherited warnings, never truncated.

(2) lib/migrate/ids.js: ver_<16hex of sha256(documentId + bodyHash)> (content-addressed, so the same id always means the same body), rel_mig_<hash of the list>, draft_hash and published_hash with ids stripped (an unchanged tenant has 0 dirty documents). All async.

(3) Existing rows (reconcile report, read-only): for each mapped document, whether a documents row already exists by id or by (type, entity_id) (phase-3 random ids are reused, never duplicated), whether its draft differs from the legacy-derived draft (it will be kept as a 'kept' version, never lost), and any slug collision with a documents row of another id (a refusal state). Existing product/collection live rows are listed.

(4) cms_templates: not mapped (blueprints are DOC-09, P1); the report counts them per family and says where they stay reachable (P4-ED05's read-only 'saved templates' page).

(5) Output: {documents, list (the v4 envelope with m), bodies (Map versionId -> body), liveRows, refs, report, sourceHash}. sourceHash is a stable hash of every legacy source row the mapping read (CUTOVER compares it to the rehearsal's). The entity part calls lib/migrate/map-entities.js, which this item creates as a stub returning empties (OVL07 owns it in batch 3). Live rows come from P4-LIVEROW's liveRowFor once map-entities fills bodies.

(6) scripts/migrate-documents.js --tenant X --dry-run [--json] [--store-open|--not-launched] (replaces SCAFFOLD's stub).
The default output is a plain-words report a non-developer can act on (lib/migrate/report.js renders it), in this order:
- one verdict line: 'Ready to move' or 'Not ready: N things to fix', each fix named in founder words with where to fix it;
- 'What shoppers will see change' (expected: nothing; each exception named by page or product);
- 'Unpublished changes that will carry over as drafts' and 'Drafts kept as older versions', named by page;
- 'Things the new editor will flag' (inherited warnings, by page);
- 'Old addresses that couldn't be matched';
- 'Saved templates' (count, and where they stay reachable);
- 'Team access that changes': the cart offer moves from upsells.write to storefront.write and storefront.publish, so the staff role (lib/platform/authz.js:19-20: upsells.write and storefront.write, no storefront.publish) can still edit the cart offer but needs an owner or admin to publish it.
Developer detail goes below a 'Details' line, and in full with --json:  the mapping, unresolved refs, sections that would change, per document the sections failing strict validation, types holding content without an editor (typeHasEditor, cartEditable from lib/registry/editability.js, never LIVEROW code), refusal states (pending schedule, live read error, cms_approvals rows or agency grants: DOC-13 not built, slug collisions, missing 'no release' flag), the reconcile report, the cms_templates count, the in-process data check result (below), and estimated backfill and flip statement counts. Both outputs end with the dry-run digest, a hash of the full JSON report whatever the output format, which CUTOVER requires. Refuses non-file URLs unless --hosted --confirm <tenantId> (owner only: a real dry run reads real data).

(7) In-process data check (non-entity part): build candidateSource({list, bodies}) through P4-SEAM and compare every non-entity resolved* getter against the legacy source's output for the routes in recordOutputs; differences are listed. OVL07 adds the entity getters.

(8) A fixture shows that a running hero experiment still serves the same hero on the migrated home (heroVariantSettings), with no payload rewrite.

Tests use P4-FIXTURES builders.

Common rules for every phase 4 item (from PLAN.md section 0): work only in your own worktree on your branch; never edit lib/preview-sessions.js, lib/sanitize.js, lib/documents/after-commit.js or scripts/drills/p3/* (import them only); never run anything against a hosted or real tenant (every CLI refuses non-file, non-localhost URLs unless given --hosted plus the extra proofs CUTOVER defines, and builders never pass --hosted); no new npm dependencies; never write to Shopify; plain words in every founder-facing message (no codes, table names or ids). Your packet docs/cms-reviews/<ID>.md has Known limits, From review and Owner checks; never edit MANUAL-CHECKS.md. Your suite already exists as a placeholder registered by P4-SCAFFOLD: replace its body, do not add package.json entries (package.json is SCAFFOLD-only; if you truly need a new script, record it as a Known limit for the orchestrator).

(1) The v4 reader uses the live rows. Whenever src.v === 4 (a live v4 release OR a SEAM candidateSource), these getters read the entity row from src.entityRows when given, else through new contentRowFor(productId) / collectionRowFor(collectionId) in lib/catalog/effective.js:
- resolvedProductOverride -> {modules, badge} from product_content_live;
- resolvedPdpPairs -> the live pairs (title and ids), then the automatic strip with legacy semantics;
- resolvedSurfaceTemplateFor('pdp', productId) -> layout_template, else doc_product_layout; a template that is not live renders the default and logs;
- resolvedCollectionPins and the collection template from collection_content_live; lib/cms/section-data.js home rails use the pins.
legacy-release.js is untouched and never reads live rows.

(2) Product and collection draft preview, WITHOUT a heartbeat (no heartbeat or overlay column exists, and lib/preview-sessions.js is not edited): when the request has a valid documents preview session (the existing contentSource preview path), the product page merges that product's documents.draft over its effective row in the page layer, and the collection page does the same for its collection_content draft. They stay in NOT_OVERLAID for the list overlay. The cart, search and sitemap stay on the live tables even in preview. Record the deviation from spec 8.9's 'only when open in the editor'.

(3) lib/migrate/map-entities.js (replaces MAPPER's stub) maps: product_overrides modules to rich_text sections {title, html} (carried verbatim, over-limit with warnings) and the badge; pdp_pairs placements to pairs {title, products} using the FIRST ENABLED placement by position per source product (lib/cms/placements.js:93-104 semantics), disabled placements never published, extra placements reported; surface_templates.products to template; collection_overrides pinned and surface_templates.collections to collection_content. v1 reads the live tables; v2/v3 read the frozen arrays. Bodies plus liveRows built with P4-LIVEROW's liveRowFor(body) (the same function publish uses), so title, description and image columns stay null. Ids reuse existing (type, entity_id) rows.

(4) The entity half of the MIG-02 data check in lib/migrate/check.js: compare resolvedProductOverride, resolvedPdpPairs, resolvedSurfaceTemplateFor and resolvedCollectionPins for EVERY product and collection with legacy content, legacy source vs candidateSource({list, bodies, entityRows}) where entityRows are either the mapped liveRows (dry run) or read back from product_content_live (after backfill, before the flip). Module HTML that the current sanitizer would rewrite shows up as a difference here.

